  "name": "Motor-EPM · embed · CORRIDOR · HEADING P+7 · COMMIT · RANGEFINDER",
  "description": "embed_corridor + HEADING-HOLD-TO-SPAWN (P=heading_bearing_hold_gain=+7.0 on the dead-reckoned bearing, D=heading_hold_gain=0.3; POSITIVE=go-straight; P-sweep{5,7,10,14}→P=7 straightness 0.53 + variance collapse) + progress→commit=1.0 (seizes a found push). HEIGHT is now MARKOV-COMPLIANT: height_topic=reality.proprio.ground_clearance (belly ToF rangefinder, NOT the god's-eye chassis_y_norm) + height_k=0.30 (was 0.65 — the flat-ground setpoint slammed the integrator at the tucked-spawn low clearance → startup flips). The height homeostat WINDUP was fixed in code (2026-07-23): height defense now fades with forward progress (height_rest_frac 1@rest→0 while moving) so it defends standing height at REST but yields to locomotion (a lift bias on the incline hoists the legs off the slope → traction loss). RESULT seed-avg: flat net_z +3.48/straight 0.67/falls 0.00; teleport-to-hump clears it (final_z +4.11, all seeds, vs the old ~2.6 stall). God's-eye is BLIND to the belly grounding so it can't solve the hump; the rangefinder senses it. Toggle [P] trail. gym_mode=corridor.",
